[Music]  with its outstanding movie score and  unique characters disney's moana became  a beloved disney animated movie in 2016.  after many years of rumors it's now time  to talk about a potential sequel in  today's original we speculate about the  possible plot of a sequel movie or a  series format of course not without  recalling the events of the first part  beforehand  the story revolves around 16 year old  moana who lives as the daughter of chief  tui on the paradisiac island of montanui  in the southern pacific together with  the other residents they worshiped te  fiti the goddess of nature who many  centuries ago was instrumental in  bringing third life to the surrounding  ocean for this purpose she used to so  called punamu stone the source of her  power unfortunately maui a demigod from  maori mythology is after the stone the  demigod of the wind and the sea is a  true master of shape-shifting and wants  to use the punamusto not for the  flourishing of the ocean but for the  creation of mankind in a fateful attack  by the volcano demon tikka maui loses  not only his giant fishhook but also the  stoneheart of the goddess of nature just  under a millennium later our eponymous  heroine moana is finally born when she  is 16 years old a terrible epidemic  ravages montanui which not only causes  the vegetation to wither but also  reduces the stock of all fish and sea  creatures to an alarming level through  her grandmother she sees some sailboats  equipped with a characteristic drums in  a hidden cave she also learns that her  people were traditionally voyagers  before maui stole the heart of te fiti  after that the sea was no longer safe as  the blessing of the punamu stone was  responsible for eliminating the dangers  of the high seas grandmother tala  finally gives her granddaughter the  fabled heart of te fiti and tells moana  on a deathbed that she must find maui in  order to restore defeat his heart moana  eventually embarks on a journey to track  down maui and convinces him to return to  fit his heart together what follows is a  journey of the two on the open sea until  they finally reach te fiti's island they  free the goddess who's trapped in the  form of the volcano monster tikka in the  end moana returns to her island where  the inhabitants welcome her joyfully and  finally go to sea again after a long  time  in addition to a possible sequel fans  are especially looking forward to this  series which has been announced at the  disney investors meeting in 2020 as  disney announced back in january this  will be available on the in-house  streaming service disney plus according  to collider the series will tie directly  into the events of the movie from 2016  however since it won't be released until  later in 2024 there's of course very  little information in the following we  speculate about what could happen in  moana 2 or the upcoming series and how  this story could continue at the end of  moana we see the villagers set sail  together and explore the newly opened  white ocean the inhabitants will  therefore very likely to find new  islands to populate under the guidance  of moana even though it has always been  her big dream to be on the high seas and  lead her sailboat sooner or later she  will have to settle down at the  beginning of the movie moana's father  prepares her for the future role as  chief at that time she was not quite  convinced of the idea as she always  wanted to sail out to sea despite her  father's warnings however after the fate  of the island has significantly changed  for the better one of the main themes  will surely be moana's new function as  chief of motonui certainly she has a  completely different style of leadership  and as already mentioned may rule over a  much larger empire than her father one  of her tasks could be to teach the  inhabitants and any newcomers the art of  sailing which has been in her blood for  many generations nevertheless we believe  that motanui stays as the most important  island in the moana series because it's  just too beautiful to look at also not  to be forgotten as a reunion of moana  and maui after the two had a somewhat  bumpy start they developed a friendship  in the end so it's a safe bet that we'll  see maui again in some form maybe they  will have to fight a big enemy again or  maui will even become a resident of  moana's home island montenui it could  also be that maui after years of  isolation finally explores the big wide  world and enjoys his newlywed freedom  either way we sure to see the two of  them in action once again the same goes  for the two sidekicks pua and haihai the  water loving house pig and the peculiar  rooster are sure to cause a few laughs  even though they do not play a leading  role in the story moana's grandma tala  who is one of the most endearing  characters of all will certainly be seen  in flashbacks after all she taught her  granddaughter many things and later even  appeared as a stingray her spirit gives  moana tips repeatedly and accompanies  her on her way similar to a guardian  angel through her one could also tell  more of the history of island nation  after all talon knows a lot about  pastimes the ocean will play another big  role as we can already see from moana's  childhood she has always had a very  special connection to the ocean and the  element of water in the end the ocean  even actively supports her which is why  we believe that the title character will  interact even more with the ocean  whether this can be compared to real  superpowers is left undecided but  there's still a lot of room for a story  an exciting question would be why did  the ocean choose moana as the chosen one  the final question is a crucial one who  will be the villain and the moana sequel  at the end of the movie it turned out  that the volcano monster tekka is just  the goddess defeated without a heart  this means there is no villain in the  story so far which is why there is an  urgent need to introduce an antagonist  the possibilities are endless we could  very well imagine an evil deity or an  antagonist to the demigod maui  theoretically the giant crab could also  be a big antagonist after all in a  post-credit scene we see him trying to  escape from his shell  in addition there are some other wild  and really creative theories out there  which would have strong implications for  moana too and therefore we present them  despite their abstruseness the best  known one says that moana is dead for  almost the whole first movie according  to that she died by the storm at the  beginning and is only revived by te fiti  and sent back to her home island alive  fans want to have found some evidence  for this for example that she doesn't  interact with normal people after the  storm passed also she experiences things  on her journey that a normal person  would never and she keeps meeting her  grandma tala and other ancestors before  she sees her as a stingray but doesn't  interact with her until after the storm  what impact this theory would have on a  sequel is of course difficult to  estimate but we didn't want to the  preview of this interesting train of  thought  now let's talk about the cast and  production of moana 2. it's pretty  likely that almost all characters and  the dubbing actress will return because  anything else would be a big letdown for  fans who else but wayne johnson should  voice the maui the demigod unfortunately  nothing is known about moana 2 yet but  as disney announced via twitter david g  derek jr the storyboard artist of  ancanto and moana will direct the  upcoming series for the first time we  can only hope that the animation style  and score will be as good as the  original fans of the moana series can  look forward to release in the course of  2024 a release window for the moana 2  movie is however not yet known  that's it again with our latest original  what do you think where exactly will the  series start and who could be the  villain we're also interested in whether  you would prefer to see the rest of the  moana story in a movie or a series  format after all both seem to play a  role at disney feel free to write us in  the comments see you next time  [Music]  you

